{
  "id": "affective-concordance",
  "term": "affective concordance",
  "definition": "Affective concordance is the tendency for partners to share or mirror emotional states, so that influences on one person’s feelings can affect the other’s mental state. In couples, this emotional linkage may support positive behaviours but can also be associated with problems such as depression or anxiety.",
